<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8f65bb30cf56f0bc5ab2cbffddaebc0713b3ee529909213c8770a633549b3a1</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Lower Saxony local polls in focus after AfD win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4772622ca95de400465a3f0f13a746a896cfeeb94d9385e46bac139a1f40bfaa</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-lower-saxony-local-polls-in-focus-after-afd-win/live-79223427--1dd3f476214d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-lower-saxony-local-polls-in-focus-after-afd-win/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The northwestern state of Lower Saxony is holding local elections that are being seen as a gauge of support for the far-right AfD party. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian GRU spies behind failed Leipzig attack: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5412c154609485fb576b786c8291c2cd8146f392197c7c3f2574f9b30f022eb7</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858--97143d694fa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German newspaper has cited reports tying a failed attack at Leipzig Airport to Moscow's GRU military intelligence agency. One suspect's ties to GRU were known when he entered the country, yet he was not surveilled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8823d33e6ead0bfb5d2efca9d2265d581069f753497d0b24f7fe5f095473c315</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
